Review the distinct completed foreground Profile sessions recorded by self-improvement. Follow the
Curator skill: use source session evidence, call native memory_write only for concise durable
entries prefixed [learned], and create or patch only Curator-managed Profile-local skill-only
packages after recurrence across distinct sessions. After creating a package, call the in-process
`profile_extensions` tool with `action: "add"` and its shelf ID. Never shell into `ziggy`, invoke
a Ziggy CLI command, or edit `extensions.json` directly; claim admission only from its
structured success result, and reopen the Profile to apply it. Log an applied or no-op decision
with self_improvement_log, and clear readiness only after the review succeeds. Do not modify
repository, catalogue, human-owned, external, or pinned packages.
